To enable advertising alternate labeled IPv6 paths via BGP while preserving primary forwarding, configure:

```console
configure router bgp
    neighbor <ip-address>
        family label-ipv6
        add-paths
            label-ipv6 send 2
        exit
        advertise-inactive
    exit
exit
```

### Explanation:
1. **`family label-ipv6`**: Ensures labeled IPv6 routes are exchanged with the neighbor.
2. **`label-ipv6 send 2`**: Advertises up to 2 best/alternate paths per labeled IPv6 prefix.
3. **`advertise-inactive`**: Allows advertising non-optimal (inactive) routes without affecting local forwarding decisions.

Replace `<ip-address>` with the neighbor's actual IP. The router will advertise multiple labeled paths while using only the optimal path for its own forwarding.
