To prevent route reflection loops within a defined BGP cluster on your Nokia 7750 SR, use the `disable-client-reflect` command on the group or neighbor associated with the cluster peers. This stops the router from reflecting routes back to the client that originally advertised them.

**Configuration Commands:**
```cli
configure router bgp group "CLUSTER_GROUP_NAME"
    disable-client-reflect
```

Replace `"CLUSTER_GROUP_NAME"` with the name of your BGP group containing the cluster peers. If applied to a specific neighbor instead, use:
```cli
configure router bgp group "CLUSTER_GROUP_NAME" neighbor <PEER_IP>
    disable-client-reflect
