To configure how the router resolves next-hops for unused private IPv4 and IPv6 routes in the base routing table, use the following CLI commands. This sets up a filter to control which tunnel types are considered for BGP route resolution:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        next-hop-resolution
            shortcut-tunn
                family ipv4
                    resolution filter
                    resolution-filter ldp rsvp
                exit
                family ipv6
                    resolution filter
                    resolution-filter ldp rsvp
                exit
```

### Key details:
1. **`resolution filter`** enables selective tunnel binding based on your defined filter
2. **`resolution-filter`** specifies allowed tunnel types (e.g., `ldp` and `rsvp` in this example)
3. Configured separately for both IPv4 and IPv6 families

Adjust the `resolution-filter` parameters to include your preferred tunnel types from these options:  
`bgp`, `ldp`, `rsvp`, `sr-isis`, `sr-ospf`, `sr-policy`, or `sr-te`.
