To configure BGP on your Nokia 7750 SR to aggregate link-bandwidth extended communities for IPv4 routes during re-advertisement with next-hop-self, use the following commands:

```cli
/configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
```

**Explanation:**  
- The `link-bandwidth` command enables the context for handling link-bandwidth extended communities.  
- `aggregate-used-paths ipv4` sums the bandwidth values from multipath routes into a single link-bandwidth extended community when readvertising IPv4 routes with `next-hop-self`.  

**For EBGP peers:**  
If readvertising to **EBGP peers**, add the `send-to-ebgp ipv4` command to permit sending the aggregated link-bandwidth community:  
```cli
/configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        link-bandwidth
            aggregate-used-paths ipv4
            send-to-ebgp ipv4
```

Replace `<group-name>` with your BGP peer group name. Apply this configuration to groups or neighbors where `next-hop-self` is used for route readvertisement.
