        disable-client-reflect
    exit
exit
```

Replace `"RR_CLIENT_GROUP"` with the name of your BGP group containing the route reflector clients.  

**Important Notes**:  
1. This command **disables all route reflection** to clients in the specified group. Ensure clients in this group do not require routes from other cluster members.
2. Verify your `cluster` configuration is correctly set (e.g., `cluster <cluster-id>`) to ensure standard route reflector loop prevention is active.  

If you need to apply this selectively to a specific neighbor instead of the entire group, use this neighbor-level configuration:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group "RR_CLIENT_GROUP"
        neighbor <IP_ADDRESS>
            disable-client-reflect
        exit
    exit
exit
```
