To enable the exchange of encrypted overlay routes (VPN-IPv4 and VPN-IPv6) between your partner networks via BGP, apply these CLI configuration commands to your Nokia 7750 SR BGP neighbor or group settings:

```
configure router bgp
    group <PARTNER_GROUP_NAME>
        neighbor <PARTNER_NEIGHBOR_IP>
            family vpn-ipv4
            family vpn-ipv6
            advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6
```

### Key details:
1. **`family vpn-ipv4` and `family vpn-ipv6`**  
   Explicitly enables the VPN address families for encrypted route exchange. Without these, VPN prefixes won't be advertised or accepted.

2. **`advertise-ipv6-next-hops vpn-ipv4 vpn-ipv6`**  
   Forces VPN routes to use IPv6 next-hops when sent over IPv6 transport sessions. This is required for proper next-hop handling with extended NH encoding (RFC 5549). Ensure partners also support this capability.

### Verification:
