To adjust BGP path prioritization on your Nokia 7750 SR and favor routes from a specific provider, configure the `local-preference` attribute at the neighbor or group level. Higher local-preference values prioritize routes. Here's the CLI configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "Preferred-Provider-Group"
        neighbor <Preferred-Peer-IP>
            local-preference 200
        exit
    exit
    group "Backup-Provider-Group"
        neighbor <Backup-Peer-IP>
            local-preference 100
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Explanation:**  
- Replace `"Preferred-Provider-Group"` and `"Backup-Provider-Group"` with your actual group names.  
- Replace `<Preferred-Peer-IP>` and `<Backup-Peer-IP>` with the IP addresses of the BGP neighbors.  
- Routes from `Preferred-Peer-IP` (local-preference `200`) will be prioritized over routes from `Backup-Peer-IP` (local-preference `100`).  

**Notes:**  
- Apply this at the **neighbor level** (as shown) for per-peer granularity.  
- If all peers in a group share the same priority, apply `local-preference` directly under the **group level** instead.  
- Values (`200`/`100`) are examples—adjust them based on your priority hierarchy.  

**Verification:**  
