To minimize delay in propagating IPv6 multicast VPN route updates when multicast group changes occur, configure the BGP session to reduce the minimum route advertisement interval. Apply this at the neighbor level for targeted control:

```cli
configure router bgp group <group_name> neighbor <neighbor_ip> min-route-advertisement 1
```

**Key details:**  
- Replace `<group_name>` and `<neighbor_ip>` with your BGP group and neighbor IP.  
- Setting `min-route-advertisement` to `1` second allows near-instant updates (down from the default 30 seconds).  
- This applies to all address families on the session.  

For MVPN-specific optimizations, enable add-paths to negotiate multiple path advertisements per MVPN IPv6 prefix if needed:  
```cli
configure router bgp group <group_name> neighbor <neighbor_ip> add-paths mvpn-ipv6 send <send_limit> receive
```  
Replace `<send_limit>` with the maximum paths per prefix (e.g., `8`).
