To configure the BGP hold time with a maximum of 2 minutes (120 seconds) and a minimum acceptable threshold of 1 minute (60 seconds) for a specific BGP neighbor, use the following commands:

```
configure router bgp
    group <group-name>
        neighbor <ip-address>
            hold-time 120 min 60
```

### Explanation:
- **`hold-time 120`**: Sets the proposed hold time to 120 seconds (2 minutes).
- **`min 60`**: Specifies the minimum acceptable hold time (60 seconds) from the peer. If the peer proposes a value below 60 seconds, the session is rejected.

### Key Notes:
1. This configuration applies directly to the specified BGP neighbor (`<ip-address>`) under the group `<group-name>`.
2. The router will propose a 120-second hold time but accept negotiated values down to 60 seconds.
3. The keepalive timer (default 30 seconds) is automatically adjusted to one-third of the **negotiated** hold time (e.g., 40 seconds for 120 seconds, 20 seconds for 60 seconds). No manual keepalive adjustment is needed.

### Example for Peer at 192.0.2.1 in Group "CORE":
```
configure router bgp
    group CORE
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            hold-time 120 min 60
```
