To ensure BGP prioritizes SR-based paths from the OSPFv3 instance with the numerically smallest priority value, configure the BGP `label-preference` command under the relevant BGP group or neighbor context. Set the `label-preference` value lower than the default (170) to make these paths more preferred:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "OSPFv3_LOW_PRIORITY_GROUP"
        label-preference 100
exit
```

**Key points:**  
- Replace `"OSPFv3_LOW_PRIORITY_GROUP"` with the BGP group name receiving paths from the OSPFv3 instance with the smallest priority.  
- The value `100` must be lower than the label preference of other OSPFv3 instances (e.g., set higher values for instances with larger priorities).  
- Routes from this group will now be prioritized for BGP next-hop resolution.  

To revert to default behavior:
```cli
configure router bgp
    group "OSPFv3_LOW_PRIORITY_GROUP"
        no label-preference
exit
```
