To add the third IPv6 address for BGP optimal route reflection, use the following CLI commands. Replace `<location-name>` with your specific location name and ensure the address `2001:db8::3` is correctly configured under the ORR location context:

```cli
configure router
    bgp
        orr
            location <location-name>
                secondary-ipv6-address 2001:db8::3
``` 

This command adds `2001:db8::3` as a secondary address in the BGP ORR location configuration, allowing it to be considered during route reflection. Note that if a secondary address already exists, this command will replace it. If you need to preserve existing addresses, reconfigure all addresses together (primary, secondary, and the new secondary) under the location.
